421 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (To ignite a passion for STEM in the next generation of our community, we conducted our fourth annual Robotics and Coding Camp, providing 256 local students with skills in 3D Modeling, circuitry, Python, and Java. Students applied these skills to a prototyped robot. Pursuing global expansion, we established six international robotics clubs in Ghana, Dubai, and India, enabling 673 students to experiment with differential drive robots with the help of virtual Webot simulations. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (Recognizing the lack of robotics programs available in schools, we implemented a district-wide robotics elective with the Alameda County Board of Education, providing students with FIRST-specific curricula including learning modules, team activities, and assessments. We open-sourced our engineering, programming, and AI curriculum via HeroX, a crowdsourcing organization, which has been shared with 2 million students and 43 educational centers.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
