435 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (Just 3 years ago, our team had only 2 girls, prompting our commitment to girls in STEM. Understanding the difficulty of having quality impact on distant regions, we harnessed collaboration in our FIRST for Girls in STEM initiative. We organized 18 teams across the US, China, India, and Spain to come together to collectively bring STEM to young girls in unique educational opportunities. We have conducted summer camps, workshops, and online events for 207 female students.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (Recognizing a gap in STEM accessibility, we expanded our mission to more underserved communities. We partnered with the California Deaf School of Fremont, not merely to host workshops, but to share STEM education to the hearing-impaired. Our team focused on teaching the fundamentals of circuitry in a uniquely adapted for  the deaf students. Our team members even learned ASL to enrich the experience for everyone involved.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
endobj
